damentals carry the forecast", "Early campaign activity is primary-focused and does not move general-election expectations"], "rationale": "Massachusetts' durable fourteen-point Democratic lean and the absence of any Republican incumbency make the Democratic nominee a clear favorite in the general election. With no general-election polling or expert ratings available, the forecast rests on the state's strong partisan fundamentals.", "watch": "Early general-election polling, a polarizing nominee on either side, or a major national shift could move the margin considerably once the campaign takes shape.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No expert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Massachusetts enters the 2028 presidential contest as one of the most Democratic states in the country, with a partisan lean of roughly fourteen points toward the Democrats. The incumbent Republican president is term-limited, so neither side benefits from incumbency, and the state's electoral votes are unlikely to be seriously contested short of a national shift.\n\nAttention so far centers on the party primaries rather than the general election. Democratic hopefuls are drawing early polling interest across New England, while Massachusetts Republicans report the most enthusiasm for Marco Rubio in the 2028 field. No general-election polls or expert ratings are available yet, so expectations rest on the state's durable partisan makeup, which points to a comfortable but not guaranteed Democratic margin.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9396, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8954, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8937, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8913, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.8966, "margin": 14.0},